r  to a dark brown tone and that will solve  most of our problems  so as a basic explanation halation takes  place in areas of high contrast usually  between sky and Dark Shadow so what I've  done here actually is I've boosted the  power and the contrast of the secondary  glow to make sure the hellish will show  up even in areas of lower contrast like  between branches for example and reduce  the spread to a minimum so it's not  bleeding all over the place making it  present over the whole image but in a  very subtle way also I've changed the  initial color of the halation effect  which was very bright and vibrant the  darker shade of orange and that is meant  to solve the color brightness problem  while also giving natural tone down  halation effect  it's looking great already some people  like this kind of a look and they can  stop right here but for a more natural  and organic look let's continue with a  couple Minor Adjustments hit a die layer  reflection bring down the strength just  by a bench and you can bring up the  gamma to increase solution in areas of  lower contrast  that's your choice  you can also adjust the spread level  even more to reduce or increase the  bleeding of the resolution effect  and there is also relative spread which  can be shown by checking this box he  here you can balance out individual  color channels like red green and blue  favoring one over the other will make it  more dominant but we'll leave this for  another video  next and final steps  in the isolation submenu set the  Threshold at your desired level each  clip will require a different threshold  level since each clip will have a  different highlight point so adjust it  your own liking and depending how much  of the image you want affected by the  Revelation lastly film saturation this  is again your personal choice but I  would recommend going for something very  subtle from 0.10 to 0.35 I've included  these settings in my cine Rec 16  millimeter film print together with more  refined color adjustments that will give  you authentic film look which can be  used on any kind of footage Rec 709 or  log 10 bit and even 8-bit I've tested it  on the new area Alexa 35 cinema camera  and it looks great you can go check out  that video I put a link in the upright  Corner if you like these settings give  this video a like and share it with  people all my field packs come with  multiple color palette variations to  give you more options to choose from and  you can find a power grid on my website  go check it out Link in description down  below you can also download the basic  Note 3 which has violation settings in  it or other free Luts on my website so  this is it for the video till next time  have fun and take care see ya  [Music]

